   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "MASKED EDIT\n\n1. Load your photo, right-click it > Open in MaskEditor, paint over the part you want to change, Save.\n2. In the prompt, describe only that part.\n3. Press Run.\n\nThe painted area is cut out with some context, edited at 1 MP (small parts get far more detail), and stitched back. Every pixel outside the mask stays exactly as it was.\n\n6 GB settings (tested on a 6 GB graphics card with 16 GB of RAM): int8 model and text encoder, the 8-step speed LoRA (8 steps, CFG 1, deis_2m: needs the RES4LYF nodes; or pick euler), comfy kitchen attention, pictures scaled to 1 MP. First run of the day is slower while the files load.\nLicence: Qwen Image 2.1 is under the Qwen Research License (non-commercial)."
